 **The Scene card's Pictures** (its picture button, `scene_pictures` in the settings file) are laid out as ZBrush for iPad's Subtools card. The Scene card's head holds Find, Add (the shapes, a voxel sphere, cages, each content pack's meshes, Import mesh and the lights), Pictures and More (Rename, All low and All high, which show every object at its lowest or highest subdivision level, Copy, Paste, Duplicate, Convert to voxels or to a mesh, Delete, Delete other and Delete all). With Pictures on, each object has a tall row: a picture of it, its name with its boolean switch under it (on makes it a Subtract in booleans; the row's menu picks Add, Subtract or Intersect), and at the right its polypaint toggle and its eye. A folder's row shows a folder with how many objects are in it, its name, a chevron that folds it and its eye. The pictures are drawn from the front, turned as the object is, in a light clay with its polypaint; one is drawn again once its object has stayed unchanged for 0.4 s, never during a stroke or while the view moves and at most one a frame, so sculpting costs nothing until the stroke ends and then one draw of the object (a full draw of a 10M-vertex object, about 20M triangles, once). A tap on a row selects it (Shift or Ctrl + tap, or Select several, adds it); a long press (or right-click) opens its menu: on the selected object Rename, Copy, Paste, Duplicate, Bring to top, Send to bottom, New folder, Make a ghost, Boolean process (Off, Union, Subtract, Intersect), Delete and Delete other; on another object only Boolean process, which leaves the selection alone. A folder's long press opens the folder menu, which also shows or hides the polypaint of every object in it. To move a row, hold it until its menu opens and then drag it (the menu closes): a line shows where it goes, as in the Scene card, and near the list's ends it scrolls along; a quick swipe scrolls the list instead. With a mouse a row drags at once. The eye works as in the Scene card (dragging down the eyes sets each row's), and the polypaint toggle leaves the object's colours out of the drawing without losing them (saved with the scene). The bar under the list sets how tall the list is, for this run. Copy keeps the object as the scene file stores it (for a 10M-vertex object about 370 MB, which the log notes), so Paste (one undo step) works after the object is deleted or in another scene; Bring to top and Send to bottom move it to the ends of its folder, or of the list, as one undo step each; Delete other and Delete all are one undo step that brings every object back, and are refused with a note when the copies undo keeps would pass the History's limit for them. All low and All high are not undo steps, as choosing a level is not. Scripts: `copy_object`, `paste_object`, `object_to_top`, `object_to_bottom`, `delete_other_objects`, `delete_all_objects`, `all_lowest_level`, `all_highest_level`.
 
